  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strategic Response Facility</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DFID Ghana will manage a small &#xa3;1.8 million Strategic Response Facility (SRF).  DFID may need to enter into agreements with third party organisations, directly contract local or international experts, or directly fund events or visits to complement the work of the Technical Service Provider. It is expected that expenditure through the SRF will be higher in the first year and decrease in subsequent years. The SRF will be managed by the Lead Adviser (Private Sector Development) and deployed with SRO approval, against a clear set of pre-agreed criteria (see Management Case for detail).</narrative>
  </description>
